      "type": "textInfo",
      "position": { "x": 1700, "y": 200 },
      "data": {
        "text": "Block Header & Proof-of-Work — Genesis Block (Block 0)\n\nA Bitcoin block header is exactly 80 bytes, composed of 6 fields:\n  1. Version (4B LE) — block version rules\n  2. Previous Block Hash (32B) — links to the previous block\n  3. Merkle Root (32B) — commits to all transactions\n  4. Timestamp (4B LE) — seconds since Unix epoch\n  5. nBits (4B LE) — compact difficulty target\n  6. Nonce (4B LE) — the field miners iterate to find a valid hash\n\nMining = hashing the 80-byte header repeatedly with different nonces until\nthe resulting double-SHA256 hash is ≤ the target. Try changing the Nonce\nnode below and watch the hash and meets_target result update.",
        "fontSize": 14
      }
    },
